## Component Structure Guidelines

### Avoid Superfluous Wrappers

- **Remove unnecessary wrapper divs**: Don't create wrapper divs that add DOM complexity without benefit
- **Simplify component structure**: Remove redundant nesting when possible
- **Keep meaningful wrappers**: Retain wrappers that serve styling, semantic, or layout purposes

### Spacing Guidelines

- **Avoid `space-*` utilities**: Don't use `space-x-*` or `space-y-*` — they rely on margin-based spacing
- **Use flex/gap spacing**: Use `flex flex-col gap-*` for vertical spacing and `flex items-center gap-*` for horizontal spacing
- **Maintain visual consistency**: Spacing changes should preserve the intended layout

## Core Components

### App (root)

- **Uses**: `usePoisonGame`; renders Header, Body, Footer
- **State**: Lifted via `usePoisonGame`: poisonRhythm, measures, New/Reuse handlers

### Body

- **Purpose**: Main game composition and soft-disabled focus guidance for New
- **Renders**: GameControls, PoisonSection, MeasuresSection, PlayControls

### GameControls

- **Purpose**: Difficulty slider and help modal
- **Uses**: Section, DifficultySlider, Modal, difficulty-level helpers

### PoisonSection

- **Purpose**: Show the current poison rhythm and New/Reuse controls
- **Props**: `poisonRhythm`, `onNewPoison`, `onReusePoison`, optional soft-disable focus helpers
- **Uses**: Section, MeasureGrid, ControlButtons

### MeasuresSection

- **Purpose**: Empty state or measure carousel
- **Props**: `measures: RhythmMeasure[]`, `poisonRhythm: RhythmMeasure | null`
- **Uses**: Section, MeasureSlider

### MeasureSlider

- **Purpose**: Carousel over measures; advances during measure playback; stops when the poison rhythm completes
- **Props**: `measures: RhythmMeasure[]`, `poisonRhythm: RhythmMeasure | null`
- **Uses**: CarouselNavButtons, CurrentMeasureDisplay, `useMetronome` (`setPlaybackMeasure`, `measureCycle`, `stop`)

### MeasureGrid

- **Purpose**: Render one measure (16th-note grid) with optional playback highlighting
- **Props**: `measure: RhythmMeasure`, `playback?: boolean`
- **Uses**: MeasureCell; `.grid-cols-16` from `src/index.css`

### Section / SectionTitle

- **Section**: Wrapper with title, optional `headerAction`, children; border, padding, gap
- **SectionTitle**: Section heading used inside Section

### Settings (layout/settings)

- **SettingsOverlay**: Settings modal body; composes ThemeSetting and SoundSetting
- **SettingsSection**: Titled settings group on a SettingsPanel surface
- **SettingsSectionTitle**: Section heading with a gray rule under the title (parallel to SectionTitle)
- **SettingsPanel**: Bordered surface utility for grouping settings controls
- **ThemeSetting**: Theme preference chips plus caption
- **SoundSetting**: Metronome and rhythm-sound mute rows (both wired via `ThemeProvider`)
- **Fieldset**: Shared `<fieldset />` wrapper with `name`, optional `legend`, and a11y props
- **SegmentedControl** / **SegmentButton**: Exclusive option chips (`aria-pressed`)
- **SettingRow**: Label-left / control-right row
- **IconToggle**: On/off icon chip built on SegmentButton
- **MuteToggle**: SettingRow + IconToggle for mute state
- **FieldCaption**: Described-by caption under a control
- **Lookups**: `lib/theme-options.ts`, `lib/mute-preferences.ts`, `settings/theme-segments.ts`

## Guidelines

- **TypeScript types**: Prefer `type` over `interface` for props
- **Named exports**: Use `export function` or `export const` for components
- **Props**: Define a single props type per component (e.g. `MeasureSliderProps`)
- **Variants over className**: Do not accept `className` on shared components for styling customization. Use a `variant` prop for supported visual differences (e.g. `ControlButton`, `AboutPoisonRhythmButton`)
- **Imports**: Use barrel imports where available; otherwise `@/lib/...`, `@/types/...`, `@/contexts/...`
- **Type imports**: Keep `import type { ... }` on separate lines from component/value imports; do not mix inline `type` into value import statements

## Typography

- **Typographic apostrophe**: Use ’ instead of ' in all user-facing text

## Accessibility

- **Buttons**: Use `<button type='button'>` for actions; set `disabled` when not applicable
- **Labels**: Use clear, descriptive text and `aria-label` for icon-only controls
- **Contrast**: Use theme color utility classes (`text-black` on `bg-surface`/`bg-surface-muted`/`bg-chrome`, `text-white` on `bg-primary`, `text-black` on page/modal surfaces, `text-dark`/`text-mid` for body copy) and shared helpers from `lib/control-classes.ts` — see `.cursor/styling.mdc`
